{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1477329-relic-lacrosse-stick","id":1477329,"title":"Relic Lacrosse Stick","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-25T07:58:22-07:00","id":1477329,"title":"Relic Lacrosse Stick","content":"So, as the title implies, I'm trying to come up with a Relic lacrosse stick for a Manitou character. This is my first attempt at Relic design in 2e, so I could use some feedback on the mechanics and dot rating.<br /> <br /> If anyone is unfamiliar, a lacrosse stick is a piece of sporting equipment that consists of a handle a few feet long, and a head with a netted pocket that is used scoop, catch and throw the ball.<br /> <br /> For the base (non-legendary) item, I think it makes sense to stat it as a weapon, giving it the tags Arcing, Bashing, Ranged and Versatile. I figure the Versatile tag works to indicate that it's generally more effective than simply catching and throwing a ball with one's bare hands. A real lacrosse stick is also a &quot;melee weapon&quot; of sorts, used to check other players or strike their sticks, but I figure the Ranged tag still makes sense in the same way that a pistol is a ranged weapon even though you can technically pistol-whip someone with it too.<br /> <br /> I think the best way to represent the lacrosse stick's special function of catching projectiles is with a special tag which I'm going to call Catching. A Catching weapon allows the user to access a special Defensive Stunt: Catch.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Catch (difficulty 1):</i> If an appropriate ranged attack against you fails to hit, you may catch the projectile and use it as ammunition to make an attack on your next turn. Generally, an attack may be caught if it is a physical object no more than fist-sized and propelled at approximately throwing speed such as a ball, rock or hand grenade. You can only hold one caught projectile at a time.</div> <br /> I figure that the Catching tag should probably have a cost of 0 since it won't provide a mechanical benefit under most circumstances, and what little benefit it does provide is balanced out by the weapon's need for ammunition at times when there is nothing to catch.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Crosse of the First-Born (oo)</b><br /> <br /> The game that is now known as lacrosse may be the oldest organized sport in North America, originating in games that were played by the First Nations of the land long before colonization. As much a religious rite as a competeition, games might last several days, played on a field miles long by teams of a thousand men or more. Naturally, the games played by the gods themselves are no less epic in scope or scale. Ranging across the entire overworld, they are played over land and sea and even in the sky. The sticks used by the gods are resilient and imbued with divine power to suit mighty immortals playing the Creator's Game.<br /> <br /> This relic resembles a nineteenth-century lacrosse stick, a shaft of hickory wood bent into a wide loop with netting woven from deergut. The handle is carved with images of birds. While wielding the Crosse of the First-Born, a Scion may imbue one point of Legend to gain the ability to apply the Catch Defensive Stunt to any ranged attack of up to her own size, regardless of its speed or composition: bullets, javelins, fire or bolts of lightning might all be caught and fired back. Scions with an appropriate Title might perform a Feat of Scale to catch an even larger projectile. Where appropriate, attacks caught and returned by the Crosse have the same tags and special effects as the original caught attack.</div> <br /> I priced this Relic at two dots because the nearest comparison I can find for the power is the Immortal Warrior Knack &quot;Hurl to the Moon.&quot; In some ways, this power is more versatile, but in some ways it's significantly more limited too, so I figure it balances out around two dots. If I wanted a more powerful version, I might up it to four dots and add a general Enhancement 1 to defense rolls against ranged attacks. If anyone has any feedback on the mechanics or dot rating, I'd be very grateful. Thanks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-25T13:59:04-07:00","id":1477357,"title":"","content":"I have no real feedback but I think it\u2019s an awesome idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}